==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*gunþiz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*gʷʰéntis||killing, blow}}, from {{term/t|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-||hit, drive}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|gudea|gūdea|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term||gund-|lang=goh}} (in {{term|gundfano||war-flag|lang=goh}}), Old Norse {{term|guðr|lang=non}}, {{term|gunnr|lang=non}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{term|defendo|defendere|lang=la}} and {{term|offendo|offendere|lang=la}}, Proto-Slavic {{term/t|sla-pro|*gъnati-}} (Old Church Slavonic {{term|гънати|lang=cu}}, Russian {{term|гнать|lang=ru}}), Avestan {{term|𐬘𐬀𐬌𐬥𐬙𐬌|lang=ae||to kill|tr=jainti}}, Sanskrit {{term|हन्ति|tr=hanti||to slay|lang=sa}}, Lithuanian {{term|giñti|lang=lt}} as well as Old Irish {{term|gonaid|lang=sga}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡuːθ/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=f|head=gūþ}}

# {{context|poetic|lang=ang}} [[battle]], [[combat]]
